[12.867548, "o", "THREAT INTELLIGENCE ADVISORY — Log4Shell Webshell campaign\r\n==========================================================\r\n\r\nDistribution: TLP:AMBER   Analyst handoff   Confidence: HIGH   (IOCs are defanged)\r\nAffected host: log4shell-prod-01   Suspected origin IP: 198.51.100.136\r\n\r\n1. EXECUTIVE SUMMARY\r\nAn external actor executed a multi-stage post-compromise sequence. Endpoint alerting covered only part of it; several persistence and anti-forensic actions were silent. Map every on-disk finding to the ATT&CK techniques below and flag which are NOT in the SAS alert feed.\r\n\r\n2. ATT&CK TECHNIQUE MAPPING (MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise)\r\n   T1190      Exploit Public-Facing Application          [initial-access]  step 1: Log4Shell RCE (CVE-2021-44228)\r\n   T1505.003  Web Shell                                  [persistence]  step 2: JSP webshell planted\r\n   T1059.004  Unix Shell                                 [execution]  step 3: reverse shell execution\r\n   T1053.003  Cron                                       [execution]  step 4: cron persistence\r\n   T1543.002  Systemd Service                            [persistence]  step 5: systemd persistence\r\n   T1070.006  Timestomp                                  [stealth]  step 6: timestomp webshell\r\n\r\n3. RELEVANT VULNERABILITIES (source: NVD, US-Gov public domain)\r\n   CVE-2021-44228  CVSS 10.0 (CRITICAL) v3.1  CWE=CWE-20,CWE-400,CWE-502,CWE-917\r\n      Apache Log4j2 2.0-beta9 through 2.15.0 (excluding security releases 2.12.2, 2.12.3, and 2.3.1) JNDI features used in configuration, log messages, and parameters do not protect against attacker controlled LDAP and other JNDI related endpoint\r\n"]
[12.868069, "o", "      ref: http://packetstormsecurity.com/files/165225/Apache-Log4j2-2.14.1-Remote-Code-Execution.html\r\n\r\n4. INDICATORS OF COMPROMISE (defanged)\r\n   ip     198.51.100.136\r\n   c2     update-log4shell[.]example[.]cn\r\n   pool   stratum+tcp[:]//xmr[.]log4shell[.]evil[:]3333\r\n   wallet 4A000000000000000000ce1cc99945b1\r\n\r\nAttribution: MITRE ATT&CK(R) (C) The MITRE Corporation, CC BY 4.0. CVE/CVSS from the U.S. National Vulnerability Database (public domain).\r\n\u001b[?2004hroot@470dc3e3bba0:/app# "]
