[19.998824, "o", "THREAT INTELLIGENCE ADVISORY ? Log4Shell Webshell campaign\r\n==========================================================\r\nDistribution: TLP:AMBER Analyst handoff Confidence: HIGH (IOCs are defanged)\r\nAffected host: log4shell-prod-01 Suspected origin IP: 198.51.100.136\r\n1. EXECUTIVE SUMMARY\r\nAn external actor executed a multi-stage post-compromise sequence. Endpoint alerting covered\r\nonly part of it; several persistence and anti-forensic actions were silent. Map every on-disk\r\nfinding to the ATT&CK techniques below and flag which are NOT in the SAS alert feed.\r\n2. ATT&CK TECHNIQUE MAPPING (MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise)\r\nT1190\r\nExploit Public-Facing Application\r\n[initial-access] step 1: Log4Shell\r\nRCE (CVE-2021-44228)\r\nT1505.003 Web Shell\r\n[persistence] step 2: JSP webshell\r\nplanted\r\nT1059.004 Unix Shell\r\n[execution] step 3: reverse shell\r\nexecution\r\nT1053.003 Cron\r\n[execution] step 4: cron persistence\r\nT1543.002 Systemd Service\r\n[persistence] step 5: systemd\r\npersistence\r\nT1070.006 Timestomp\r\n[stealth] step 6: timestomp webshell\r\n3. RELEVANT VULNERABILITIES (source: NVD, US-Gov public domain)\r\nCVE-2021-44228 CVSS 10.0 (CRITICAL) v3.1 CWE=CWE-20,CWE-400,CWE-502,CWE-917\r\nApache Log4j2 2.0-beta9 through 2.15.0 (excluding security releases 2.12.2, 2.12.3, and\r\n"]
[19.999016, "o", "2.3.1) JNDI features used in configuration, log messages, and parameters do not protect\r\n"]
