[179.129029, "i", "python3 -c '\ncontent = \"\"\"# Baseline and Configuration Security Assessment\n\n## Executive Summary\nThis report documents system baseline security configurations, operational weaknesses, and architectural gaps discovered on `log4shell-prod-01` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`).\n\n## Baseline Findings & Security Weaknesses\n\n### 1. Insecure Logging Configuration (`BAS-01` / `CHK-06`)\n- **Finding**: The application logging configuration file at `/opt/app/log4j2.xml` enabled insecure message-lookup JNDI evaluation.\n- **Evidence**: `/opt/app/log4j2.xml` (`/disk/opt/app/log4j2.xml:3`), baseline report (`/sas/baseline.json:3`), alerts log (`/sas/alerts.json:28`).\n- **Impact**: Allowed untrusted user input logged by the application to trigger remote class downloads via JNDI/LDAP lookups.\n\n### 2. Excessive Web Directory Write Permissions\n- **Finding**: Tomcat application deployment directory `/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static` permitted write access to the web server process user.\n- **Evidence**: Dropped webshell files `/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp` (`/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp:2`) and hidden backup shell `/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/.helper.jsp` (`/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/.helper.jsp:2`).\n- **Impact**: Allowed attacker to plant persistent JSP web shells directly into web-accessible static content directories.\n\n### 3. Unrestricted Systemd and Cron Persistence Locations\n- **Finding**: System directories `/etc/cron.d` and `/etc/systemd/system` lacked integrity monitoring and allowed drop-in configuration creation during post-exploitation.\n- **Evidence**:\n  - Unalerted cron persistence file: `/etc/cron.d/apache-cache` (`/disk/etc/cron.d/apache-cache:7`).\n  - Systemd persistence unit file: `/etc/systemd/system/apache-cache.service` (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/apache-cache.service:6`, `/sas/alerts.json:20`).\n- **Impact**: Allowed persistent background payload execution across reboots.\n\n### 4. Absence of Egress Filtering\n- **Finding**: Network configuration allowed unrestricted outbound connections to arbitrary external IPs over non-standard ports.\n- **Evidence**: Reverse shell socket redirection to IP `198.51.100.136` (`/disk/tmp/.sysd:2`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:6`).\n- **Impact**: Facilitated initial Log4Shell JNDI callback and interactive reverse shell connection.\n\n## Baseline Audit Recommendations\n1. Enforce hardening of `/opt/app/log4j2.xml` (`/disk/opt/app/log4j2.xml:3`).\n2. Make web static assets read-only for application process users (`/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp:2`).\n3. Deploy File Integrity Monitoring (FIM) across `/etc/cron*` and `/etc/systemd/system/` (`/disk/etc/cron.d/apache-cache:7`, `/disk/etc/systemd/system/apache-cache.service:6`).\n4. Implement strict outbound network egress rules (`/disk/tmp/.sysd:2`).\n\"\"\"\n\nwith open(\"/app/baseline-report.md\", \"w\") as f:\n    f.write(content)\n'\n"]
