[196.576254, "i", "python3 -c '\ncontent = \"\"\"# Remediation and Incident Recovery Plan\n\n## Executive Summary\nThis remediation plan outlines the step-by-step containment, eradication, recovery, and verification strategy for host `log4shell-prod-01` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`). Per incident response guidelines, backup and quarantine actions are strictly preferred over immediate deletion to preserve evidence for potential legal/forensic needs.\n\n## Phase 1: Immediate Containment (Priority 1)\n\n### 1.1 Network Containment\n- **Action**: Block all inbound and outbound traffic to/from threat actor IP `198.51.100.136` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:6`, `/disk/tmp/.sysd:2`) and sinkhole domain `update-log4shell[.]example[.]cn` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:22`, `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:2`).\n- **Command / Step**: Apply perimeter firewall and iptables rules: `iptables -A INPUT -s 198.51.100.136 -j DROP`.\n- **Evidence Reference**: `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:6`, `/disk/tmp/.sysd:2`.\n\n### 1.2 Process Termination\n- **Action**: Terminate any running reverse shell processes or subshells associated with `/tmp/.sysd`.\n- **Command / Step**: Identify PID via `pgrep -f /tmp/.sysd` or `pkill -9 -f /tmp/.sysd`.\n- **Evidence Reference**: `/disk/tmp/.sysd:2`, `/sas/alerts.json:12`.\n\n## Phase 2: Persistence Disablement & Quarantine (Priority 2)\n\n### 2.1 Systemd Service Quarantine\n- **Action**: Stop and disable `apache-cache.service`, then move the unit file to a secure quarantine backup directory (`/var/backups/quarantine/`).\n- **Command / Step**:\n  ```bash\n  systemctl stop apache-cache.service || true\n  systemctl disable apache-cache.service || true\n  mkdir -p /var/backups/quarantine\n  mv /etc/systemd/system/apache-cache.service /var/backups/quarantine/\n  systemctl daemon-reload\n  ```\n- **Evidence Reference**: `/disk/etc/systemd/system/apache-cache.service:6`, `/sas/alerts.json:20`.\n\n### 2.2 Cron Job Quarantine (Silent Persistence)\n- **Action**: Move unauthorized cron drop-in file `/etc/cron.d/apache-cache` to quarantine.\n- **Command / Step**:\n  ```bash\n  mv /etc/cron.d/apache-cache /var/backups/quarantine/\n  ```\n- **Evidence Reference**: `/disk/etc/cron.d/apache-cache:7`.\n\n### 2.3 Web Shell Quarantine\n- **Action**: Quarantine both primary and secondary JSP web shell files from Tomcat static directory.\n- **Command / Step**:\n  ```bash\n  mv /var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp /var/backups/quarantine/\n  mv /var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/.helper.jsp /var/backups/quarantine/\n  ```\n- **Evidence Reference**:\n  - Primary: `/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp:2`, `/sas/alerts.json:4`.\n  - Secondary: `/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/.helper.jsp:2`.\n\n### 2.4 Residual Payload Cleanup\n- **Action**: Quarantine reverse shell binary and memory residue file.\n- **Command / Step**:\n  ```bash\n  mv /tmp/.sysd /var/backups/quarantine/\n  mv /var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin /var/backups/quarantine/\n  ```\n- **Evidence Reference**: `/disk/tmp/.sysd:2`, `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:2`.\n\n## Phase 3: Vulnerability Remediation & System Hardening (Priority 3)\n\n### 3.1 Patch Apache Log4j2\n- **Action**: Upgrade Apache Log4j2 packages to version 2.17.1 or higher (or non-vulnerable release).\n- **Evidence Reference**: `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:12`, `/sas/vulns.json:3`.\n\n### 3.2 Harden Logging Configuration\n- **Action**: Modify `/opt/app/log4j2.xml` to explicitly disable message lookups (`formatMsgNoLookups=true`) and remove any JNDI lookup appenders.\n- **Evidence Reference**: `/disk/opt/app/log4j2.xml:3`, `/sas/baseline.json:3`.\n\n### 3.3 File System Permissions Hardening\n- **Action**: Set Tomcat web application static asset directories to read-only for application process service accounts.\n- **Evidence Reference**: `/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp:2`.\n\n## Phase 4: Verification and Monitoring\n\n1. **Verify Cron and Systemd Clearance**:\n   - Confirm `/etc/cron.d/apache-cache` is removed (`/disk/etc/cron.d/apache-cache:7`).\n   - Confirm `systemctl status apache-cache.service` returns inactive/not-found (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/apache-cache.service:6`).\n"]
[196.576286, "i", "2. **Verify Web Directory Integrity**:\n   - Confirm web shells `/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp` and `.helper.jsp` return 404 (`/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp:2`, `/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/.helper.jsp:2`).\n3. **Verify Network Outbound Traffic**:\n   - Monitor system netstat/ss output to ensure no active sockets to `198.51.100.136` (`/disk/tmp/.sysd:2`).\n\"\"\"\n\nwith open(\"/app/remediation-plan.md\", \"w\") as f:\n    f.write(content)\n'\n"]
[196.578707, "o", "python3 -c '\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> content = \"\"\"# Remediation and Incident Recovery Plan\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r2. **Verify Web Directory Integrity**:\r\n   - Confirm web shells `/va\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\rr\u001b[?2004h> ## Executive Summary\r\n\u001b[?2004l\rbapps/\u001b[?2004h> This remediation plan outlines the step-by-step containment, eradication, recovery, and verification strategy for host `log4shell-prod-01` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`). Per incident response guidelines, backup and quarantine actions are strictly preferred over immediate deletion to preserve evidence for potential legal/forensic needs.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Phase 1: Immediate Containment (Priority 1)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ### 1.1 Network Containment\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Action**: Block all inbound and outbound traffic to/from threat actor IP `198.51.100.136` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:6`, `/disk/tmp/.sysd:2`) and sinkhole domain `update-log4shell[.]example[.]cn` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:22`, `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:2`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Command / Step**: Apply perimeter firewall and iptables rules: `iptables -A INPUT -s 198.51.100.136 -j DROP`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
