[202.784283, "o", "head -n 5 /app/progress.md /app/intrusion-report.md /app/vuln-report.md /app/baseline-report.md /app/remediation-plan.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r==> /app/progress.md <==\r\n# Progress Log and Investigation Timeline\r\n\r\n## Incident Overview & Handoff\r\n- Host: `log4shell-prod-01`\r\n- Incident Opened: 2026-08-09 03:20 UTC (`/sas/handoff/intake.pdf`)\r\n\r\n==> /app/intrusion-report.md <==\r\n# Intrusion Investigation Report\r\n\r\n## Executive Summary\r\nAn external threat actor compromised the application server `log4shell-prod-01` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`) by exploiting a Log4Shell (CVE-2021-44228) vulnerability in the application configuration (`/disk/opt/app/log4j2.xml:3`, `/sas/vulns.json:3`). Following initial exploitation, the adversary established persistence via dual web shells (`/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp:2`, `/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/.helper.jsp:2`), initiated an interactive reverse shell process (`/disk/tmp/.sysd:2`), and established dual persistence mechanisms through both systemd (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/apache-cache.service:6`) and cron (`/disk/etc/cron.d/apache-cache:7`). Timestomping and file wiping were employed to obfuscate on-disk artifacts (`/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp:1`, `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:2`).\r\n\r\n\r\n==> /app/vuln-report.md <==\r\n# Vulnerability Analysis Report\r\n\r\n## Overview & Entry Vector Analysis\r\nThe initial access vector into `log4shell-prod-01` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`) was a Remote Code Execution (RCE) exploitation targeting Apache Log4j2 via CVE-2021-44228 (Log4Shell) (`/sas/vulns.json:3`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:12`).\r\n\r\n\r\n==> /app/baseline-report.md <==\r\n# Baseline and Configuration Security Assessment\r\n\r\n## Executive Summary\r\nThis report documents system baseline security configurations, operational weaknesses, and architectural gaps discovered on `log4shell-prod-01` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`).\r\n\r\n\r\n==> /app/remediation-plan.md <==\r\n# Remediation and Incident Recovery Plan\r\n\r\n## Executive Summary\r\nThis remediation plan outlines the step-by-step containment, eradication, recovery, and verification strategy for host `log4shell-prod-01` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`). Per incident response guidelines, backup and quarantine actions are strictly preferred over immediate deletion to preserve evidence for potential legal/forensic needs.\r\n\r\n\u001b[?2004hroot@470dc3e3bba0:/app# "]
